/**
@page elements_animation Animation Elements

\details Declarative SVG animation elements recognized by the default parser.
Use `SVGDocument::setTime()` to select a sample and render the document; Donner has no animation
clock of its own. The editor's Preview mode advances this clock and dispatches pointer events.
Secure static documents do not animate, and secure animated documents run authored timing but
reject host events and scheduling. \ref GettingStartedAnimation shows how a host drives the clock.

Clock, event, syncbase and repeat timing are supported, together with linear, discrete, paced and
spline interpolation. Host applications can schedule begin/end instances and query lifecycle events
without executing script. CSS Animations, JavaScript, wall-clock/access-key bindings and destructive
`<discard>` behavior are outside this profile.

See [the animation support matrix](design_docs/animation.md) for rendered attribute coverage.

- \subpage xml_animate
- \subpage xml_animateTransform
- \subpage xml_set
- \subpage xml_animateMotion
- \subpage xml_mpath
*/
